---
import { SitePage } from '@boombapbot/editor';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base
  title="Docs · boombapbot"
  description="How to use РИТМ-12, the boombapbot drum machine: writing patterns, accents, recording by tapping, swing, the sound knobs, the effect and exporting."
>
  <SitePage client:load baseUrl={base} current="docs">
    <h1>How to use РИТМ-12</h1>
    <p class="sb-lede">
      Press the play key and it plays. Everything else on the panel changes what it plays or how it sounds. The
      lettering is Russian, so this page gives each control as it is lettered and says what it is.
    </p>

    <h2>The idea</h2>
    <p>
      The machine remembers four <strong>patterns</strong>: А, Б, В and Г. A pattern is one measure of sixteen
      steps. It has a row for each of the eight instruments and one row of accents, and each step in a row is on
      or off.
    </p>

    <h2>Writing a pattern</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Press the play key, the first of the three under <strong>УПРАВЛЕНИЕ</strong>. The pattern goes round.</li>
      <li>
        Press an instrument key on the left, under <strong>ИНСТРУМЕНТЫ</strong>. It plays the sound and selects
        it, and its lamp stays lit.
      </li>
      <li>
        Press the step keys, the row of sixteen under <strong>СЕКВЕНСЕР</strong>, where it should play. A lit
        key is a step that is on; press it again to turn it off.
      </li>
      <li>Choose another instrument and carry on. The step keys always show the instrument that is selected.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>The instruments</h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>БАС</dt>
      <dd>Kick.</dd>
      <dt>МАЛЫЙ</dt>
      <dd>Snare.</dd>
      <dt>ХЛОП</dt>
      <dd>Clap.</dd>
      <dt>ХЭТ З and ХЭТ О</dt>
      <dd>Closed hat and open hat. Each one cuts the other off.</dd>
      <dt>ТОМ</dt>
      <dd>Tom.</dd>
      <dt>РИМ</dt>
      <dd>Rim.</dd>
      <dt>ПЕРК</dt>
      <dd>Percussion.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h3>Accents</h3>
    <p>
      The <strong>РЕЖИМ ЗАПИСИ</strong> switch decides what the step keys write. On <strong>УДАРЫ</strong> they
      write hits of the selected instrument. On <strong>АКЦЕНТЫ</strong> they write the pattern's accents. Every
      instrument that plays on an accented step is louder, by as much as the <strong>АКЦЕНТ</strong> knob says.
    </p>

    <h3>Recording by tapping</h3>
    <p>
      Press the record key, the one with the red dot, while the pattern plays. Now each instrument key you
      press in time is written on the step it lands on. Press record again to stop. Everything tapped in one go
      is one undo step.
    </p>

    <h3>Mute, dice and clear</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>МУТ</strong> silences the selected instrument and leaves its steps where they are.</li>
      <li>The key with the die writes a new row for the selected instrument, by chance.</li>
      <li><strong>СБРОС</strong> empties the pattern you are on. Undo brings it back.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Patterns, measure and tempo</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>ПАТТЕРН</dt>
      <dd>
        The keys А, Б, В and Г choose the pattern you see and hear. Pressed while the machine plays, the new one
        takes over at the end of the measure.
      </dd>
      <dt>РАЗМЕР</dt>
      <dd>
        The length of a measure, for all four patterns. <strong>16</strong> is sixteen steps, four to the beat.
        <strong>12</strong> is twelve steps of triplets, three to the beat, and the last four step keys sit out.
      </dd>
      <dt>ТЕМП</dt>
      <dd>From 40 to 300 beats a minute. The screen shows the number.</dd>
      <dt>СВИНГ</dt>
      <dd>Plays every second step late, from not at all up to a hard shuffle. Triplets do not swing.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>The sounds</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The knob beside each instrument key is that instrument's level.</li>
      <li>
        The three knobs under <strong>ОБРАБОТКА ГОЛОСА</strong> work on the selected instrument:
        <strong>ПИТЧ</strong> is its pitch, <strong>ЗАТУХАНИЕ</strong> how long it rings, and
        <strong>ТОН</strong> how bright it is. Each instrument keeps its own settings.
      </li>
      <li><strong>ГРОМКОСТЬ</strong> is the volume of the whole machine, and the <strong>УРОВЕНЬ</strong> meter shows how loud it is.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Drag a knob up or down to turn it, or focus it and use the arrow keys. The screen says what the control
      you just touched did.
    </p>

    <h2>The effect</h2>
    <p>
      There is one effect on the whole machine. Press the <strong>ЭФФЕКТ</strong> selector to step to the next
      of four: <strong>ДИЛЭЙ</strong> is an echo, <strong>РЕВЕРБ</strong> a reverb, <strong>ФЛЭНЖЕР</strong> a
      flanger and <strong>ХОР</strong> a chorus. The <strong>СМЕСЬ</strong> knob sets how much of it you hear.
      At 0 there is none.
    </p>

    <h2>Keeping what you make</h2>
    <p>
      Everything is saved in this browser as you go. The cog in the footer opens settings, where you can name
      your beat, undo and redo, put the starter patterns back, clear one pattern or everything, and import or
      export. With a free account you can also save up to 20 beats to it from the account button in the footer,
      and load them on another device.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Project file</strong> holds everything the machine remembers, and opens here again.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>WAV and MIDI</strong> hold the pattern you are on, as a loop of one measure. The WAV has the
        effect in it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What comes with it</h2>
    <p>A new machine has a beat on А and a busier turn of it on Б. В and Г are empty.</p>

    <h2>Beats from the earlier machine</h2>
    <p>
      boombapbot used to be a different machine. A beat made on it opens here as a РИТМ-12 beat, whether it is
      the draft in this browser, a project file or a beat saved to your account. The rhythm that machine was on
      becomes pattern А, and a notice lists what did not fit.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing old is written over. The earlier draft stays in this browser, and a beat in your account stays as
      it was: saving the one that opened here adds a new beat beside it.
    </p>

    <h2>On a phone</h2>
    <p>
      The picture is wider than the screen, so scroll it sideways, or press <strong>Fit to screen</strong> under
      it to see the whole machine at once. A strip under the picture chooses the instrument, and a play button
      stays docked at the bottom.
    </p>

    <h2>Keyboard</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt><kbd>Space</kbd></dt>
      <dd>Start or stop.</dd>
      <dt>Arrow keys</dt>
      <dd>Move between step keys, and turn the knob that has focus.</dd>
      <dt><kbd>Enter</kbd></dt>
      <dd>Press the key that has focus.</dd>
      <dt><kbd>Esc</kbd></dt>
      <dd>Close a window.</dd>
      <dt><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> or <kbd>Cmd</kbd> + <kbd>Z</kbd></dt>
      <dd>Undo. Add <kbd>Shift</kbd> to redo.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>The power switch</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>СЕТЬ</strong> turns the machine off: it goes dark, it stops, and nothing else on it answers until
      you switch it back on. Nothing it remembers is lost.
    </p>
  </SitePage>
</Base>
